<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Session ended — @BRAND_NAME@</title>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<link rel="icon" href="./assets/brand-logo.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
<style>
  /* Lato is served from this directory rather than Google Fonts: the container
     runs under an egress allowlist, and this page is also reached when the
     desktop behind it is gone. Nothing here may depend on the network. */
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Lato';
    src: url('./assets/brand-body.ttf') format('truetype');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Lato';
    src: url('./assets/brand-body-bold.ttf') format('truetype');
    font-weight: 700;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  :root {
    --accent: @COLOR_ACCENT@;
    --accent-hover: @COLOR_ACCENT_HOVER@;
    --secondary: @COLOR_SECONDARY@;
    --muted: @COLOR_MUTED@;
    --surface: @COLOR_SURFACE@;
    --surface-raised: @COLOR_SURFACE_RAISED@;
    --text: @COLOR_TEXT@;
    --text-muted: @COLOR_TEXT_MUTED@;
    --font: '@FONT_FAMILY@', 'Open Sans', 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, sans-serif;
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    min-height: 100vh;
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  main {
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    border-radius: 14px;
    border-top: 4px solid var(--accent);
    box-shadow: 0 6px 28px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.09);
    max-width: 26rem;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 2.5rem 2rem 2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .logo { width: 76px; height: 76px; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }

  h1 {
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  p { font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0 0 1.75rem; }

  .actions { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.625rem; }

  .btn {
    display: block;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    border: 2px solid transparent;
    transition: background-color 0.15s ease, border-color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .btn-primary { background: var(--accent); color: #2B2B2B; }
  .btn-primary:hover { background: var(--accent-hover); }
  .btn-secondary { background: transparent; color: var(--text); border-color: var(--muted); }
  .btn-secondary:hover { border-color: var(--secondary); }

  /* Focus must stay visible for keyboard users — WCAG 2.2 AA. */
  .btn:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--secondary); outline-offset: 2px; }


  /* The cost reminder. Deliberately not styled as an error: nothing has gone
     wrong, but a disconnected session is exactly the moment someone assumes
     they are done and walks away from a machine that is still billing. */
  .notice {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 1rem 1.125rem;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 12%, transparent);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 38%, transparent);
    text-align: left;
  }
  .notice p { font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 0.875rem; color: var(--text); }
  .notice p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .notice strong { font-weight: 700; }
  footer { margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
  footer a { color: var(--text-muted); }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --surface: #232425;
      --surface-raised: #2E2F30;
      --text: #F2F2F0;
      --text-muted: #B4B5B5;
    }
    body { background: var(--surface); }
    .btn-primary { color: #232425; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <h1>You are logged out</h1>
    <p>
      The connection to your desktop closed. Reconnecting will take you
      straight back in if your sign-in is still valid.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/">Reconnect</a>
    </div>
    <!-- Replaced at container start by qgis-desktop-manage-link, which is the
         only way a build-time artefact can carry a runtime URL. Left exactly as
         it is when QGIS_DESKTOP_MANAGE_URL is unset. -->
    <!--QGIS_DESKTOP_MANAGE_LINK-->
  </main>
</body>
</html>
